note seed/node/live-test.om -- the live coding workflow under the durable
note scheduler (DRA-399). It drives the real programs (ollm serving the own
note round40 model, code-main, code-test, tool, infer) and checks what they
note did; it implements none of their logic. Composition (omc exit status
note checked; fn main is here):
note   { printf 'om2\n'; cat seed/json/json.om om/tls/sha2.om
note     seed/node/live-test.om; } | seed/out/omc > build/node/live-test
note Usage: live-test BASE NODE OLLM MODELDIR OMC40 SEL [serve=0] [parts=fcr]
note BASE must not exist (it is created); NODE holds infer, tool, code-main
note and code-test; MODELDIR holds model.ck and merges.bin; OMC40 is the
note compiler the objectives are checked with; SEL is the round40
note final-selected.json. All paths absolute. serve=0 runs without a model
note server (negative control: every check that needs the model must FAIL
note and the exit is nonzero). parts= picks the full run (f), the
note cancellation (c) and the crash and restart (r); a part left out is
note NOT_RUN. Run it inside bwrap --unshare-net (the server listens on
note 127.0.0.1:18399). Output: LIVE, HASH, SEL, PREP, SERVE, RUN, REVIEW,
note SNAP and JOP evidence lines, one PASS|FAIL|NOT_RUN line per check, then
note "LIVE checks N pass P fail F not_run R". Exit 0 only if every check
note passed, 1 otherwise, 2 usage.
note Scenario directories BASE/full, BASE/cancel, BASE/crash each hold
note root/jobs (the files the objectives repair), work, journal (the
note node's journal v2), serve.log and the programs' stdout/stderr.

text lto0 "loop,4,3,70,jobs/item76666.om,Fix the error in this file and confirm its goal."
text lto1 "loop,5,3,71,jobs/item83423.om,Inspect the code and repair it to satisfy the goal."
text lto2 "loop,1,6,72,jobs/item82342.om,Fix the error in this file and confirm its goal."
text lto3 "loop,2,4,70,jobs/item85188.om,Fix the error in this file and confirm its goal."
text ltj0 "jobs/item76666.om"
text ltj1 "jobs/item83423.om"
text ltj2 "jobs/item82342.om"
text ltj3 "jobs/item85188.om"

